  "title": "The treble clef",
  "summary": "The clef for the right hand, curling round the G line.",
  "minutes": 6,
  "steps": [
    {
      "type": "explain",
      "title": "Treble clef",
      "body": "The curly sign at the start of the staff is a clef; this one is the **treble clef**. It curls round the second line, marking it as the G above middle C. With it, the lines from the bottom are E G B D F (\"Every Good Boy Does Fine\") and the spaces spell F A C E.\n\n**Why it matters:** Melodies and the right-hand part of piano music are written in treble clef. It is the first clef most people learn.",
